# Task 6 Fix Round 2 Re-review

**Base:** `5cebaf9`  
**Head:** `696980b`  
**Verdict:** **NEEDS FIXES — Critical 2, Important 2, Minor 1**

## Scope and method

This was a fresh read-only review of the full Fix Round 2 section of
`task-6-report.md`, the full supplied `review-5cebaf9..696980b.diff`, the open
items from `task-6-rereview-1.md`, the Task 6 contract, and the relevant current
source/tests. No tracked file was edited. No provider, network, live pricing,
real SDK, replay, Docker, background process, or permanent ledger was used.

One fake/temp reproducer was attempted solely to exercise the capability issue,
but the managed Windows ACL denied fixture setup before the manifest or any
ledger was created. The exact temporary root was removed immediately. Findings
below therefore rely on quoted control-flow evidence and precise fake/temp RED
shapes; no product test result is claimed from this re-review.

The round closes live pricing reauthentication and the advertised `Pricing`
contract. It also materially improves byte capture and nonaccepted terminal
atomicity. It is not ready because the code that labels an input
“controller-originated” is an unrestricted public issuer, the live sealed call
plan can still drift after preflight and reservation, and the durable terminal
receipt/recovery boundary is incomplete.

